==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-sell like hot cakes.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|[[sell]]<,,sold> [[like]] [[hotcake|hot cake]]s}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|idiomatic}} To be [[sold]] in large numbers [[quickly]].
#: {{ux|en|During a power outage, candles '''sell like hot cakes'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Pop Muzik|author={{w|Robin Scott (singer)|Robin Scott}}|year=1979|passage=You're living in a disco / Forget about the rat race / Let's do the Milkshake / '''Selling like a hotcake'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Jim Berkenstadt|author2=Charles R. Cross|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=No3CKSsCRQcC&pg=PA119&dq=%22sold+like+hot+cakes%22&as_brr=3#v=onepage&q=%22sold%20like%20hot%20cakes%22&f=false|title=Nevermind: Nirvana|passage=Geffen employees confirm that about half of the initial run of forty-six thousand [copies of [[w:Nevermind|Nevermind]]] went to the Northwest, where it '''sold like hot cakes'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=G. Timothy Haight|author2=Daniel Singer|title=The real estate investment handbook|passage=These units will '''sell like hot cakes''' for $400000 apiece. Our cost will be $250000. It's a regular gold mine.}}
#* '''2009''', ''John o'Groat Journal'', 27 November, "Calendar boys get their tops off"
#*: CALENDARS featuring local men willing to get their kit off for charity are '''selling like hot cakes''' after hitting the market this week.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Cosmo Knight|title=The Day After the Great Trout Run
|passage=I sold 12 trout specials yesterday, they '''sold like hot cakes'''.}}

